# demo.rpn — a guided tour of rpn's commands, each result labeled.
# Run with:  ./rpn examples/demo.rpn
# The same file runs identically under GNU dc:  dc examples/demo.rpn
# Note: p prints without popping, so standalone labels are followed by c.

[--- Arithmetic (integer scale 0) ---] p c
0 k
[2 + 3 = ] P 2 3 + p c
[10 / 4 = ] P 10 4 / p c
[5 3 ~ pushes remainder then quotient, f prints top first] p c 5 3 ~ f c
[2 ^ 10 = ] P 2 10 ^ p c
[3 v (square root) = ] P 3 v p c
[10 % 7 = ] P 10 7 % p c
[2 ^ 100 mod 1000 = ] P 2 100 1000 | p c

[] p c [--- Scale factor k ---] p c
2 k
[1 / 3 with k=2 = ] P 1 3 / p c
[5 % 3 with k=2 = ] P 5 3 % p c
[K (current scale) = ] P K p c
0 k

[] p c [--- Input and output bases ---] p c
[255 printed in base 16: ] P 16 o 255 p c
[255 printed in base 10: ] P 10 o 255 p c
[FF read in base 16: ] P 16 i FF p c
[input base I and output base O, one per line: ] p c A i I p O p c

[] p c [--- Stack operations and printing ---] p c
[stack after 1 2 3, f prints top first] p c 1 2 3 f c
[after r (swap top two)] p c 1 2 r f c
[5 d * (duplicate, multiply) = ] P 5 d * p c
[strings with P (no newline), then a number with p: ] P [ab] P [cd] P 10 p c
[z (stack depth) = ] P z p c
[123 Z (digit count) = ] P 123 Z p c
[1.50 Z = ] P 1.50 Z p c
[1.50 X (scale digits) = ] P 1.50 X p c

[] p c [--- Strings and macros ---] p c
[a macro executed with x: 2 3 + p gives ] P [2 3 + p] x c
[nested macro gives ] P [[2 3 + p] x] x c
[a string literal printed with p: ] P [hello] p c

[] p c [--- Registers and arrays ---] p c
[42 stored with sa, loaded with la = ] P 42 sa la p c
[a macro register run with x: la 1 + p gives ] P 5 sa [la 1 + p] sm lmx c
[array register A: store 1 2 with Sa, then la, La, L a] p c 1 Sa 2 Sa la p La La c f
[array a: 7 2 :a then 2 ;a gives ] P 7 2 :a 2 ;a p c

[] p c [--- Conditionals, loops, q and Q ---] p c
[countdown from 5 with a conditional macro] p c 5 sc [lc p lc 1 - sc 0 lc >m] sm lmx c
[Q stops the macro early: ] P [1 p 1 Q 2 p] x 3 p c
[6! computed with a loop = ] P 6 sn 1 sa [la ln * sa ln 1 - sn 0 ln >m] sm lmx la p c

q
